From 53e888fe7339221454d85131d4b755fdd443ce2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:31:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] feat(launcher): build the game on the device from the
 player's disc

A Linux launcher that needs no generated code (MM3_LAUNCHER_ONLY):
mm3-launcher shows a setup over the settings until the game is built
for it. The player picks a disc image (found in the home folder and on
SD cards, or chosen with the desktop's file dialog), confirms they own
it, and setup/mm3_setup.py beside the launcher checks the disc, copies
its files, translates the code and compiles the game in
~/.local/share/MidtownMadness3, reporting its steps on standard output.
Once built, the footer adds Add to Steam and Rebuild, and Play runs the
start script the setup writes, which is also what Steam and the desktop
menu start.

The start script sets MM3_LAUNCHER_SKIP: the game's own launcher then
exports the saved settings without opening a window.
